{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'yin/slot|yin/literal|packet|plain-data' docs/design/yin.vm.macro.md | head -65\"","aggregated_output":"30:   tree packet to `program-out`.\n32:   named by content address; a tree packet is `[root-address rows]`. Neither\n44:   packets and returns one tree packet. It sees no program store, captured\n88:### 1.2 Tree packet\n90:A tree packet is:\n97:Physical row order has no semantic meaning. A packet is self-contained: every\n159:positions, so paths mean the same thing on every host. `yin/slot` uses this\n184:canonical tree packets.\n223:On success, `program-out` receives exactly one tree packet:\n243:            → {:status :ok :tree tree-packet :log log-packet :ctx ctx'}\n244:            | {:status :error :error error-data :log log-packet :ctx ctx'}\n245:expand       : batch ctx → tree-packet | throws\n247:invoke       : macro-entry operand-trees ctx -> tree-packet\n248:valid-tree?  : tree-packet opts → nil | error-data\n249:mark-tail    : tree-packet → tree-packet\n268:opaque plain-data identity token for the `program-in` medium. The observer does\n277:maps a symbol to a self-contained lambda tree packet.\n283:1. **Admit.** Validate batch shape, tree packets, the closed tag vocabulary,\n288:   lambda packet; a plain occurrence removes the name whatever its value.\n337:Stand-ins may occur as working nodes in operand and result packets, never as\n375:For each packet the expander builds `address → row`. The canonical grammar\n399:Every store value is a stamped entry, `(macro-entry packet contract)`,\n400:`{:yin.macro/tree packet :yin.macro/contract c}`: a macro packet is\n402:post-harvest stamp only packets this expander produced from the batch it\n405:`expand-batch` refuse a store holding a bare packet or an entry without\n420:    operands = [subtree-packet(index, child) for child in row.operands]\n460:admitted by `valid-tree?`, and the packets harvested from them are this\n464:stamps the packets it produces with the current AST contract, and that\n493:`invoke` binds positional parameters to operand tree packets. With `[a & rest]`,\n494:`rest` is a vector of packets. Arity failure is:\n531:The prelude consumes and returns tree packets. Constructors intern canonical\n532:row bodies and return self-contained packets.\n537:| `yin/slot tree n` | Root slot at zero-based full-row position `n`; a child slot returns a tree packet. Positions `0` and `1` are invalid. |\n538:| `yin/literal value`, `yin/variable sym` | Leaf constructors. |\n548:Merging packets verifies that one address denotes one body. Packets are closed\n565:validated canonical lambda packet. There is no privileged `defn` branch.\n600:| packet is `[root-address rows]` | `{:kind :malformed-input :reason :packet-shape}` |\n616:transitional address encoding does not hash. It is checked within one packet\n631:A result must be one valid packet. It may contain canonical rows and valid\n640:`reason` is one of the §7.1 packet reasons, including `:packet-shape` for a\n641:result that is not a packet. It is `:address-conflict` when a result row\n665:Every attempt has the plain-data identity `[incarnation-token counter]`. The\n713:### 8.3 Log packet\n722:packets named by successful events, deduplicated by root address in first-use\n724:receives only the final program tree packet.\n743: :out writer          :out-staged nil|tree-packet\n744: :log writer|nil      :log-staged nil|log-packet\n803:expanded tree packet, and event rows. `(reset)` rebuilds expander and evaluator\n809:tree to rows, emits one packet per root or disconnected definition tree, emits\n823:provenance stores log packets unchanged or indexes event rows as a separate\n838:- Implement packet validation and occurrence-path navigation.\n903:6. Macro operands and results are tree packets; invocation needs no conversion.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
